Scene: AnimalLongCoat.olo
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LONG-COATED ANIMAL fixture (issue #1239).
#
# A procedurally generated quadruped whose long coat is a SOLID OFFSET
# SHELL (Models/Reference/generate_reference_animals.py).
#
# THIS IS THE CURRENT-LIMITATION BASELINE, and it is meant to look like
# one: hard silhouette, no strand detail, no anisotropic specular, no
# wind response. Issues #1232 (groom curve assets) and #1241 replace the
# shell with real curves, and this capture is what they are measured
# against. Do not 'improve' the coat here.
#
# No rigged long-coated asset is obtainable without a purchase, so this
# subject is static where the short-coated Fox animates — the moving
# sequence for this fixture comes from the manifest's camera Motion.
#
# Ground, sky and light rig are IDENTICAL to the other animal fixture, so
# the short- and long-coated captures differ only in the subject.
#
# GENERATED by OloEngine/tests/scripts/generate_reference_fixture_scenes.py
# (issue #1239) — edit the generator and regenerate rather than hand-editing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
